commentBody:
@RHUttam

Welcome! 
So glad you popped in!

@Andrzej

Yes the overlay on 17A was confusing as it appeared at first glance that only the unshaded squares were highlighted when the clue was selected. I thought it was part of the trick/theme at first. 

I also took the * clue to be part of the theme at first, but possibly that was an intentional misdirect.

@Petrol

Query on the rules of engagement for the across only challenge. 

Are you allowed to look at the words in the down direction as they form, and/or guess what they might be, or only after you have completed every across.

@JohnWM 

Our oak trees here in Atlanta are still pretty much fully leafed out, although that will change shortly. We have yet to have our first freeze here, and daytime highs have mostly been in the seventies so far.

The last thing I expect to see in a crossword puzzle clue is precision. They are usually open to multiple interpretations, which tends to make them a bit blurry.

@Claudia

Before I had the crossword subscription and was solving daily, I would get the Wednesday and Sunday puzzles for free in the Chapel Hill News (RIP).  I liked those puzzles because they were more clever and more challenging than the LA Times puzzles I was doing daily, and I could always complete the Wednesday puzzle, and almost always complete the Sunday puzzle.

Now that I solve daily, I pretty much appreciate every day of the week's puzzle, though Monday, and sometimes Tuesday, less so.
